                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "For future reference:\r\n- It was added in neovim/neovim#27361 via `scoped` extmark property.\r\n- It was removed in neovim/neovim#28728 in favor of yet experimental `nvim__ns_set()`. So it is not even yet Neovim>=0.12, I am afraid so will have to wait a bit. It is a shame because 'mini.jump2d' would also benefit from this (when there is a same buffer in a split jumping is a bit off).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">For future reference:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>It was added in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2120539711\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/27361\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/neovim/neovim/pull/27361/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/27361\">neovim/neovim#27361</a> via <code class=\"notranslate\">scoped</code> extmark property.</li>\n<li>It was removed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2291618005\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/28728\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/neovim/neovim/pull/28728/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/28728\">neovim/neovim#28728</a> in favor of yet experimental <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim__ns_set()</code>. So it is not even yet Neovim&gt;=0.12, I am afraid so will have to wait a bit. It is a shame because 'mini.jump2d' would also benefit from this (when there is a same buffer in a split jumping is a bit off).</li>\n</ul>",
                    "bodyText": "For future reference:\n\nIt was added in neovim/neovim#27361 via scoped extmark property.\nIt was removed in neovim/neovim#28728 in favor of yet experimental nvim__ns_set(). So it is not even yet Neovim>=0.12, I am afraid so will have to wait a bit. It is a shame because 'mini.jump2d' would also benefit from this (when there is a same buffer in a split jumping is a bit off).",
